      "text": "16)Open the valve and let water flow out\nof the pressure tester.\n1) Switch on coffee machine.\n2) Place a measuring cup on cup sup\nport.\nCitiz service manual  137 FUNCTION TESTS\n3) After heating up, press the \"small cup\"\nbutton for approximately 10 sec to pre\nheat the coffee outlet with hot water.\n4) Empty measuring cup and place it\nback on cup support.\n5) Insert capsule (Cosi is best suited).\n6) Press the \"small cup\" button again.\n7) Wait until the measuring cup contains",
      "section_id": "sec_007",
      "section_title": "9.5 Measure coffee temperature 15)Switch off the coffee machine.",
      "page_start": 7,
      "page_end": 8,
      "char_start": 3541,
      "char_end": 4016
    },
    {
      "text": "8) Then measure the coffee temperature\napprox. 510mm under the coffee out\nlet.\nThe coffee temperature should be\n86°C ± 3 °C (187 °F ± 5.4 °F).\nCitiz service manual  138 FUNCTION TESTS",
      "section_id": "sec_008",
      "section_title": "20 ml of coffee.",
      "page_start": 8,
      "page_end": 9,
      "char_start": 4018,
      "char_end": 4201
    },
    {
      "text": "Use newly opened UHT, full fat or semiskimmed milk at fridge temperature (+8°C till\n+10°C) for the following tests only.",
      "section_id": "sec_010",
      "section_title": "Prerequisite",
      "page_start": 9,
      "page_end": 9,
      "char_start": 4203,
      "char_end": 4323
    },
    {
      "text": "• Prepare 240 ml hot milk in milk frother (use mixer without spring).\n• Measure temperature immediately after preparation in jug.\nThe milk temperature should be between + 60 °C and + 70 °C (140 °F  till 158°F).",
      "section_id": "sec_011",
      "section_title": "9.6.1 Measure hot milk temperature",
